# qwen3.6:27b as the MINER for the McMiner pseudocode track.
#
# Why a derived model: Ollama's default context is smaller than these prompts,
# and overflow is truncated SILENTLY -- you get confident-looking misconceptions
# mined from a clipped prompt, with nothing in the logs.
#
# Why 16K. Measured on this dataset (scripts/preflight.py prints these):
#
#     arm        max prompt chars   ~tokens   + 4000-token response cap
#     baseline              6,220     1,681                      5,681
#     rag                  10,848     2,931                      6,931
#     ref                  10,585     2,860                      6,860
#     rag_ref              15,011     4,057                      8,057
#
# The true ceiling is ~8.1K tokens, so 16384 is already 2x headroom. The
# parent repo used 32768 on the assumption that a rag_ref bag ran ~10K tokens;
# it does not. That extra 16K of context bought nothing and cost ~2.7 GB of KV
# cache -- which on a memory-constrained machine is the difference between a
# partial CPU offload and a model that will not load at all.
#
# Weights are ~17 GB regardless of num_ctx. On 8 GB VRAM expect most of that in
# system RAM; see README "Hardware" for what that means in practice.
#
#   ollama create qwen3.6-mcminer -f Modelfile.qwen36-miner

FROM qwen3.6:27b

PARAMETER num_ctx 16384
